content:
I'll begin by exploring the workspace structure and reading the data files to understand what we're working with.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/offline_evaluation_metrics.csv"
  }
}
```
```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/online_ab_test_metrics.csv"
  }
}
```

Now I have both datasets. Let me create the necessary directory structure and write the analysis code.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir -p code outputs report/images"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "if not exist code mkdir code && if not exist outputs mkdir outputs && if not exist report\\images mkdir report\\images"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python analysis.py"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/analysis.py",
    "old_str": "def load_data():\n    \"\"\"Load offline and online evaluation metrics.\"\"\"\n    offline = pd.read_csv('data/offline_evaluation_metrics.csv')\n    online = pd.read_csv('data/online_ab_test_metrics.csv')\n    return offline, online",
    "new_str": "def load_data():\n    \"\"\"Load offline and online evaluation metrics.\"\"\"\n    offline = pd.read_csv('../data/offline_evaluation_metrics.csv')\n    online = pd.read_csv('../data/online_ab_test_metrics.csv')\n    return offline, online"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python analysis.py"
  }
}
```

```json
